    <briefdescription>
<para>C++20 concept satisfied when a type can be used as a test expression in <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>assume()</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type to be checked.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput>checkable</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> is either a framework operator type (derived from <computeroutput>op</computeroutput>) or is implicitly convertible to <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput>. It is used to constrain the <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>assume()</computeroutput> function templates, ensuring that only sensible expression types are accepted. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
